#: rootopts.cpp:115
msgid "Enable Desktop &Menu"
msgstr "Cho phe'p thu+.&c ddo+n desktop"

#: rootopts.cpp:117
msgid ""
"Check this option if you want the desktop popup menus to appear at the top "
"of the screen in the style of Macintosh. This setting is independent of the "
"global top-level menu setting that applies to KDE applications."
msgstr ""
"Nha^.n tuy` cho.n na`y ne^'u ba.n muo^'n thu+.c ddo+n popup desktop xua^'t hie^.n o+? "
"phi'a tre^n ma`n hi`nh gio^'ng nhu+ Macintosh . Thie^'t la^.p na`y la` ddo^.c la^.p vo+'i "
"thie^'t la^.p thu+.c ddo+n top-level toa`n cu.c ma` ddu+o+.c a'p du.ng cho ca'c u+'ng"
"du.ng KDE ."

#: rootopts.cpp:122
msgid "Enable &Icons on Desktop"
msgstr "Cho phe'p &Icon tre^n Desktop"

#: rootopts.cpp:124
msgid ""
"Uncheck this option if you do not want to have icons on the desktop. Without "
"icons the desktop will be somewhat faster but you will no longer be able to "
"drag files to the desktop."
msgstr ""
"Bo? tuy` cho.n na`y ne^'u ba.n kho^ng muo^'n co' Icon tre^n Desktop . Kho^ng co'"
"icon tre^n desktop thi` co' ve? nhanh ho+n nhu+ng ba.n se~ ma^'t kha? na(ng ke'o / tha?"
"tu+` / va`o desktop ."

#: rootopts.cpp:129
msgid "Align Icons &Vertically on Desktop"
msgstr "Do'ng ha`ng icon &tha(?ng ddu+'ng tre^n desktop"

#: rootopts.cpp:131
msgid ""
"Check this option if you want the icons on the desktop to be aligned "
"vertically (in columns). If you leave this option unchecked, desktop icons "
"are aligned horizontally.<p> Note that you can drag icons wherever you want "
"to on the desktop. When you choose \"Arrange Icons\" from the Desktop menu, "
"icons will be arranged horizontally or vertically."
msgstr ""
"Cho.n tuy` cho.n na`y ne^'u ba.n muo^'n ca'c Icon ddu+o+.c gio'ng tha(?ng ddu+'ng"
"(theo co^.t) tre^n Desktop . Ne^'u ba.n bo? tuy` cho.n na`y, ca'c desktop icon se~"
"ddu+o+.c xe^'p thao chie^`u ngang . <p> chu' y' la` ba.n co' the^? tha? icon ba^'t ki`"
"cho^~ na`o tre^n desktop . Khi ba.n cho.n \"Sa('p xe^'p icon\" tu+` thu+.c ddo+n desktop,"
"icon se~ ddu+o+.c xe^'p tha(?ng ddu+'ng hay na(`m ngang ."

#: rootopts.cpp:138
msgid "Show H&idden Files on Desktop"
msgstr "Hie^.n ca'c file a^?&n tre^n Desktop "

#: rootopts.cpp:140
msgid ""
"If you check this option, any files in your desktop directory that begin "
"with a period (.) will be shown. Usually, such files contain configuration "
"information, and remain hidden from view.<p> For example, files which are "
"named \".directory\" are plain text files which contain information for "
"Konqueror, such as the icon to use in displaying a directory, the order in "
"which files should be sorted, etc. You should not change or delete these "
"files unless you know what you are doing!"
msgstr ""
"If you check this option, any files in your desktop directory that begin "
"with a period (.) will be shown. Usually, such files contain configuration "
"information, and remain hidden from view.<p> For example, files which are "
"named \".directory\" are plain text files which contain information for "
"Konqueror, such as the icon to use in displaying a directory, the order in "
"which files should be sorted, etc. You should not change or delete these "
"files unless you know what you are doing!"

#: rootopts.cpp:150
msgid "Pr&ograms in Desktop Window"
